    {
      "id": "text-12",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Clothing Zombies",
        "body": "Each empty shell of clothing is designed to resemble human figures, creating a haunting visual as they race through the streets, embodying the idea that discarded garments continue to affect our world long after they've been thrown away.\n\n‍\n\nTo get the effects spot on, the SFX team brought in massive air-pressure cannons, which we ended up calling “anti-vacuum cannons.” These were loaded with synthetic garments and shot directly onto the set, creating a physical, interactive experience for the actors and everything around them. Clothes hit props like a bus and a car, allowing for a more realistic integration with the CGI added later.\n\n‍\n\n**Check out some behind the scenes clips:**"
      },
      "padTop": "4-5",
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
